WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.650
I don't remember much from when I was a child.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.780
I played and lived like a normal child.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.570
But I won't forget that day.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.500
On that day, something that should have not shook, shook.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.340
I saw two suns in the sky.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.090
The real sun to the east...

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.510
And in the west, there was another sun in the darkness.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:46.230
My dad murmured that a war had begun,
and my mom was praying to God.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.980
I was fascinated by it and just watched, thinking it was beautiful.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:56.780
July 1999

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.780
Huge Alien Spaceship Falls to the Earth

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:54.940
I was really a stupid kid.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.290
When we found out about extraterrestrial
life, humankind had to wake up...

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:04.790
And the world experienced a sudden change.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.750
Peace was shaken, like how the ground shook.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.220
When I took notice, I was there and fighting.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.260
It had nothing to do with the UN Government or Anti-UN Alliance.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.430
I just want to regain the Earth that doesn't shake.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.150
I know that the idea is just fantasy.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.600
<i>Purple One to all wings.</i>

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.100
Enemy Tallyho at 2 o'clock.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.210
Altitude, 3,300. Distance, 6,500.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.230
Three bogeys.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.110
Only three?

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:13.610
Let's go.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.260
Behind you!

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.240
Too slow.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:54.840
Bingo!

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.440
<i>Mayday! Mayday! Enemy on my tail!</i>

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.190
Idiot.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.280
Shin!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.920
<i>Purple One, thanks for saving me, but at least warn me
before you blast away.</i>

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.470
It's your fault for letting the enemy get behind you.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.800
<i>What did you say?!</i>

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.220
<i>Do you want more kills that badly?</i>

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.640
Shin, that's not good. We're going to lose buddies to cover our backs.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.730
I have never relied on anyone to cover my back.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.650
If I let my guard down for even a second, I'll get shot down.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.150
Does that mean you don't want me, either?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.700
I see. Oh, well...

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.850
I'm like a loser who fell in love with a gorgeous woman.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.830
I'll keep following her even if I get stepped on.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:41.020
<i>This is Ilastria. We are being attacked by an unidentified air force.</i>

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:41.710
<i>We request immediate—</i>

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.340
Ilastria, respond. Ilastria!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.310
Think about the fuel while you're flying.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.730
If our mothership goes down, fuel will be meaningless.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:00.650
What...?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.900
10 o'clock. It hid inside the cloud.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.120
No response on the radar. Yellow One, Two, can you catch it?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.870
<i>Yellow One to all wings. We're not getting a response, either.</i>

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:12.970
<i>The enemy is a stealth—</i>

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.660
<i>Yellow One!</i>

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.040
<i>It's fast!</i>

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.290
Missiles!

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.290
Flares! Flares!

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.180
Here they are...

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.600
Now!

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.780
Yes!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.950
Yellow Two, the enemy went your way!

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.740
Yellow Two!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.790
You're not going anywhere...

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:02.540
Gotcha!

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:07.760
What?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.260
A human?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:27.240
A long time ago, when this world had just begun...

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.110
The ocean and wind was there.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.120
At the time, humans were fish.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:40.250
Then, the birdman who came through the stars flew above the ocean.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:47.710
The fishman, in awe and fear of the birdman's grand wings,

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.470
said this to the birdman:

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:55.470
"You may be able to fly, but you do not know how deep the ocean is."

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.980
"How sad and pitiful," he laughed.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:09.610
The birdman got mad and cut off the tail and fins of the fishman.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.990
From the wound, legs grew.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:19.950
This is how the first human, Rooy Kanu, was born.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.030
Edgar! Edgar, are you okay?

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:54.740
Edgar!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.630
Where am I?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:27.730
Who is it?

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.320
Birds, birds, and birds.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:46.580
Who is it?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.460
Where am I?

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:54.840
I'm asking where this is.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.850
You're not supposed to point that to a man.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.180
I have something like this, as well.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.890
Do you want to buy it? I'll make it cheap.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.940
I'm asking where this is.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:09.690
Mayan.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.110
The island where the ocean and wind mixes... Mayan.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:21.120
One who fell from the sky, this is not a place you should stay.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.620
Is this an island influenced by Anti-UN Alliance powers?

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.580
I am the hand led by the wind.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:32.630
The noisy wind interrupted the holy pilgrimage. That is why I knew that...

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.300
Soldiers covered in blood would awaken.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.430
The wind will become cloudy.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:43.970
Mayan's wind will become cloudy and Kaduns will begin to live in the grass.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.400
If you have awakened, get off this island immediately.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:56.280
That's nonsense. There should have been one more guy.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.820
This is...

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:04.930
Don't touch it! Where's the other guy?!

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.700
We only found you.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.600
What?

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.500
Only one person drifted here.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:14.740
Mao.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:15.840
Watch out.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:25.850
The current here is complicated, so if he didn't
float here, maybe he was taken to the offing.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:29.140
No... Edgar...

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.020
Now that you know, take the communication ship in the afternoon.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.570
A stranger's tear of sadness will call the Kadun as well.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:36.320
What?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.680
Wait, Sis, his wound hasn't healed yet.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.000
Mao, you be quiet.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:45.810
If the blood goes into the ocean, an evil spirit, a Kadun, will come.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:48.000
It will follow the blood to this island.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.490
A Kadun that comes from the ocean is strong.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.820
You may stay here until your wounds heal.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.620
The melody of the wind says so, too.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.270
Yeah! You can stay.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.370
I'm Mao, Mao Nome.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:33.220
This is my sister Sara... Sara Nome.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.210
Shut up!

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.640
Wait!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:31.020
I believe that you are aware that CYCLOPS, a cross
dimensional radar based on a new theory...

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.770
...was able to activate because of the over-technology
that was obtained by the now destroyed Ass-One.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:42.150
As a result of that, we were able to observe a PCS response around this area that was very similar to Ass-One.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.820
The deep sea investigation team was able to confirm the object.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.950
We believe it was left behind by the aliens.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:53.000
Aliens? In this sea?

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.000
It is codenamed AFOS.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.210
Are those fragments of the Ass-One when it was shot down?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:07.720
No, the precise date is a B-1 secret matter, so I cannot give any details.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:12.220
Judging from the sea bed's abnormal magnetic materials and from the analyse of devolved...

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.040
...plankton DNA around the area...

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.700
We believe it's over 10,000 years old.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.450
Over 10,000 years old?

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.800
No way.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.240
Humanity was only in the Stone Age.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:27.360
Thank you, Doctor.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:34.160
We are currently in the retrieval process for the AFOS we found.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.590
Hello, Senpai.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.020
Focker!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.240
It's been a long time since I saw you. Welcome
to the Aircraft Carrier Asuka.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.090
What?

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.140
Look at how you're dressed...

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:53.870
Doctor?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:56.680
Oh, begin without me. I'll be there in a minute.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.230
Okay...

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:04.460
Why are you on an aircraft carrier?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.550
That goes for you, too.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.400
Se-n-pa-i.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:10.740
Geez.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:21.170
You said that you would run to Nevada or something if a war began.

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:26.840
People change, unlike a scholar's doctrine.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:32.470
Doctrines change, too. That's why I am here.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.680
Tell me, out of our old friendship...

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:43.770
Why are you, a cultural anthropology major, in a special squad?

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.740
That's a shame. The answer is a B-1 secret matter.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.610
I can't tell it to a Major-class person like you.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:58.870
Does that mean you're here to verify the human proto-culture intervention hypothesis, Aries-senpai?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.210
Roy...

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:39.870
That's why I told you to do Number Two when it's high tide.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:48.170
Hey!

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.180
Shin!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:16:00.080
Hey, what's a train? Is it true that it runs on two sticks at fast speed?

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:03.980
Hey, do buildings like these really exist? They look like mountains.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.230
This island has nothing.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.650
If it has a phone, I could contact the UN Force.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.320
And what are those strange things?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:18.970
Those are birdmen.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:24.290
Birdmen? It looks more like a plane than a bird.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:29.710
A long time ago, birdmen traveled through
the stars, came to this island...

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:35.570
...and dropped a sea turtle's shell. The shell broke,
and that became the island of Mayan.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:38.390
A sea turtle became an island, eh?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.410
Yes. It's only a legend.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:46.000
Hey, now tell me about the city you lived in, Shin.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.020
City?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.400
City, you say?

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:59.180
Why do you have a satellite antenna when you don't even have electricity?

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:00.620
I don't know.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.960
The generator died in a storm one year ago.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:05.580
A generator?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.960
It looks like it can still be used.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:13.300
Why didn't anyone fix it?

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:21.680
Because the adults who could fix them went to big cities or the army.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.270
So this is an island of women, children, and old people.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:29.690
Fine, I'll fix this.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.110
Really?

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.110
Yeah.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:34.860
Just as a thank you for helping me.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.270
Hey, what is that?

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:43.750
Oh, you mean the spear?

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.330
Boys make those.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:50.590
Everyone tries to make theirs in distinct forms so you can distinguish them.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:55.090
Then, you show others that this is what your spear looks like.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:18:01.040
Then at night, you stick that into the house
of the girl you want to date, and...

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:04.810
If it's the spear of the boy she likes, she pulls it in.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.630
Then the two go on a date at midnight.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.310
Date?

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.210
Yes. That's this island's custom.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:15.650
In other words, it's a love letter.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:31.580
I... I was threatening her with a love letter?

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.460
How stupid...

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.260
It was funnier since you were serious.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.510
I bet.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:44.390
I'm glad that you can laugh, Shin.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:54.230
Come to think of it, I wonder when the last time I laughed was...

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:06.100
According to intelligence, it is predicted that the Anti-UN Alliance will start using a new-type transforming fighter...

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:09.160
...to commence a surprise attack tomorrow morning.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:13.330
Now is the time to show the results of your training.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.170
All pilots are afraid of their first battlefield.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:22.010
However, being impatient is a taboo, just
like the first time you screw a woman.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.870
Be daring and delicate at the same time.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:25.680
That's it.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.260
Thank you for your work, Head Engineer Nakajima.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:40.900
Hey, Focker. It's finally going to be Zero's first campaign.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:41.450
Yes.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:48.830
Be careful, though. These ladies are smart, but they eat a lot of fuel.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:54.900
But then again, these super ladies have the currently
ultimate EGF-127 engine tuned to the max...

00:19:54.900 --> 00:20:03.970
...instead of the planned reactor engine that didn't make
it in time, so I guess that's the price we have to pay.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:08.100
I understand. I will use it very carefully.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.540
I'll just believe half of that.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.900
You treat women roughly.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:25.760
I thought that the SWAG energy converter-type armor that
makes use of the over-technology is as hard as a tank?

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:28.240
But you're going to pilot it.

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:37.270
But even if the plane is tough, those fledglings are going to fly them.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:42.760
Since the war was prolonged, lack of personnel has reached its limits.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:48.180
All the skilled men died.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:55.020
I will bring the VF-O and the fledglings back.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:20.110
What are you doing?

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.510
Listening to that machine's noise again.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:26.410
Why don't you remember the song of the holy pilgrimage?

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:31.010
No way. That old song? It's just a superstition.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.080
It's not superstition.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:39.560
What are you going to do if you get possessed by the cursed urban Kadun because you followed that stranger around?

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.490
Cursed urban Kadun?

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:52.950
If a visitor from the city didn't take this picture
of mom and dad, we wouldn't have this!

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:58.760
That's... But if your real memories remain within...

00:21:58.760 --> 00:21:59.960
Sis, you idiot!

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:03.670
Mao...

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:48.550
I thought I heard something weird. What are you doing here...?

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:54.560
Girls make love sticks, too?

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:57.810
Who are you going to show that love letter to?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.070
You have that many? You have that many men you want to show it to?

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:05.570
No!

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:14.410
Since you can't make that much as a maiden,
you're going to sell those as a side job.

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:49.760
I haven't told you yet...

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:50.450
What?

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:53.360
Thank you for saving me.

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:00.370
A long time ago, when this world had just begun...

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.370
The ocean and wind was there.

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:08.090
You make the spears by imagining that
you are mixing the ocean and wind.

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:14.800
I don't understand.

00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:40.580
Hey, what's wrong? Get a hold of yourself.

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.310
The wind...

00:24:43.310 --> 00:24:44.040
The wind?

00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:49.050
The wind is going to blow... And it will carry
a Kadun that will bring destruction.

00:24:49.570 --> 00:24:51.380
A terrible wind...

00:24:56.430 --> 00:24:57.470
It's coming.

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:14.110
The UN Force's new fighter...

00:25:23.730 --> 00:25:24.500
Not good enough!

00:26:23.310 --> 00:26:25.710
What is that machine?

00:26:25.710 --> 00:26:27.640
Is it a birdman?

00:26:29.290 --> 00:26:32.070
<i>Mayday! Mayday! Multiple missiles locked on to me!</i>

00:26:32.340 --> 00:26:34.110
Don't panic! I'm on my way!

00:26:37.240 --> 00:26:38.070
Watch out!

00:26:45.640 --> 00:26:46.540
Are you okay?

00:26:47.060 --> 00:26:47.980
Yes...

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:48.870
Mao!

00:27:00.680 --> 00:27:04.120
Mao went to the sacred fountain to get water...

00:27:04.120 --> 00:27:05.370
What?

00:27:05.370 --> 00:27:06.370
Where's the fountain?

00:27:06.370 --> 00:27:10.420
In this forest. Follow the mountain path and
it should be beneath that Cross Rock.

00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:12.380
Okay, I'll go get her.

00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:13.020
I will, too.

00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:15.530
No! You lead the people in the town to safety.

00:27:16.630 --> 00:27:17.490
Okay...

00:27:18.010 --> 00:27:18.950
Hurry!

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:35.210
Mao!

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:42.390
When the birdmen appear again...

00:27:44.390 --> 00:27:47.600
...a song of destruction will echo into the world.

00:27:55.650 --> 00:28:02.360
Chapter One

00:27:55.650 --> 00:28:02.360
The Ocean, the Wind, and...

